      "description": "Museum label for Soviet 122 mm howitzer Model 1909-1937, displayed in Hämeenlinna Artillery Museum. This particular gun was manufactured in St. Petersburg and Perm in 1910.  The Model 1909 howitzer was based on a German Krupp design. They were produced in Imperial Russia and then in the Soviet Union.  As was typical for most World War I artillery pieces, the gun was modernised from 1937 onwards, the resulting guns called Model 09-37.  \nPhoto taken on June 18, 2006.\n\nSource: Photo by me, User:Balcer.",
